    <string name="codex_login_disclosure_browser">Sign-in happens on auth.openai.com, in the browser, the same way as codex login. This app never sees the password or the browser\'s cookies; it only receives, on this device, a one-time authorization code.</string>
    <string name="codex_login_disclosure_client">OpenAI does not offer a sign-in for other apps, so this one uses the public sign-in client of Codex CLI, OpenAI\'s command-line tool. It does not need the device-code option in ChatGPT\'s security settings.</string>
    <string name="codex_login_disclosure_scope">Requested permissions: openid, profile, email and offline_access (account identity and renewing access); Codex CLI also asks for connector permissions this app does not use. The token belongs to your ChatGPT account and is not read-only; the app only uses it to read Codex usage.</string>
    <string name="codex_login_disclosure_storage">Tokens stay on this device, encrypted with an Android Keystore key. Disconnecting asks OpenAI to revoke the access and deletes them from the device.</string>
